From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: alpha-build <alpha-build@localhost>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 23:15:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Snap: stop force-enabling software video stabilization on
 sltexx

swVDIS (libvdis) worker is joined without timeout from stopPreview(); its
frame supply stops when the ISP reconfigures, so the join never returns:
HAL binder thread blocked -> setPreviewWindow/setParameters never answer ->
Snap ANR. Reproduced on video recording and on preview reconfiguration
(camera switch). Disabling the forced enable removes the deadlock; the only
loss is the 2014 SW image stabilizer (no gyro on this sensor anyway).

Change-Id: Id25443dd422cde94c955f3e5622882c45d9afb3d
---
 src/com/android/camera/VideoModule.java | 17 ++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/com/android/camera/VideoModule.java b/src/com/android/camera/VideoModule.java
index a1c5cfb..21a85b2 100644
--- a/src/com/android/camera/VideoModule.java
+++ b/src/com/android/camera/VideoModule.java
@@ -2973,12 +2973,19 @@ public class VideoModule implements CameraModule,
 
         mParameters.set(CameraUtil.RECORDING_HINT, CameraUtil.TRUE);
 
-        // Enable video stabilization. Convenience methods not available in API
-        // level <= 14
+        // Video stabilization is deliberately NOT enabled here (sltexx patch).
+        // On this device the HAL implements it as SOFTWARE VDIS (SecCameraSWVDIS,
+        // libvdis.so). The swVDIS worker is joined without a timeout from
+        // ExynosCamera::stopPreview() -> m_swVDIS_Release() -> vsParamFree() ->
+        // pthread_join, and the worker is starved of frames whenever the video
+        // pipeline is reconfigured (kernel shows fimc_is_scp_video_dqbuf fail(-512)).
+        // Result: pthread_join never returns, the HAL binder thread blocks, and every
+        // stopPreview deadlocks - captured in /data/anr traces 2026-11-22 22:50 and
+        // 23:12. Repro: record video, or switch cameras while the preview pipeline
+        // reconfigures. Same root cause as the long-open "front/back switch hangs".
+        // The S5K2P2 has no gyro DIS, so what we lose is a 2014 software stabilizer
+        // that crops 2176x1216 -> 1920x1080 anyway.
         String vstabSupported = mParameters.get("video-stabilization-supported");
-        if ("true".equals(vstabSupported)) {
-            mParameters.set("video-stabilization", "true");
-        }
 
         // Set picture size.
         // The logic here is different from the logic in still-mode camera.
